# Kids master lock — write the implementation plan, link it, re-star it

## Context

The 2026-08-03 feasibility research ([docs/planning/08-kids-master-lock-feasibility.md](../../Documents/BonsAI/docs/planning/08-kids-master-lock-feasibility.md))
returned **GO**: `SteamClient.Parental.RegisterForParentalSettingsChanges` exists,
is already in the tree via `@decky/ui@4.11.3`, is what Steam's own client uses,
and exposes a top-level `locked` boolean that needs no protobuf decode.

That closes the one thing the roadmap entry named as an open dependency
("a detectable Steam signal"), which is also the thing its ★★★★★ rating was
pricing in. So three artifacts are now stale and this change fixes all three:

1. There is no implementation plan — only research.
2. The roadmap entry doesn't link the research, still lists the signal as an
   open dependency, and is rated for an unknown that no longer exists.
3. At ★★★ the entry violates the roadmap's own sorting rule and no longer
   qualifies for the GitHub-placeholder convention.

No code ships in this change. It is docs + roadmap only.

## Decisions already taken (from the research + this session)

